samples: PENDING ch05/ex5-8 [run(exit=0, stdout="marmot 5")] — blocker: TWO blockers, re-measured at bs50 against wolf 0.2.15 / lupin 0.1.37, and NEITHER is the one this row used to name. (1) `sorted_by` exists now — it is one of `[type.comb.set]`'s ten — but it is a `std.list` function that must reach its home module, and this repository configures no std root for either tool, so both machines decline at `[type.method.root]`: lupin `unsupported`, wolf E0301. That half is wolf-book#39, not a std-surface debt. (2) `.take(1)` can never arrive: `take` is a keyword, so `fn take` is E0008 on both machines and no std function may carry the name. This row is waiting on a spelling that cannot exist and the exercise wants rewriting (wolf-book#58). Re-measured at bs53 against wolf 0.2.17 / lupin 0.1.40, and identically against 0.2.16 / 0.1.38: lupin `unsupported` (`List.sorted_by` reaches `std.list` and no std root is configured), exit 4; wolf no longer says E0301 — it answers `cannot compile this yet — member access on a value whose type is still being inferred` at `resolve`, exit 4. wolf-book#39 closed on 2026-09-12 with the std posture recorded in `wolf-toolchain.toml`; its open successor is wolf-book#45. Re-measured at bs54 against wolf 0.2.18 / lupin 0.1.41, and identically against 0.2.17 / 0.1.40 the same hour: both answers unchanged, word for word, at the same span (@300..303). Re-measured at bs55 against wolf 0.2.19 / lupin 0.1.42 and 0.2.18 / 0.1.41 the same hour: identical on both pairs, word for word, same span. Re-measured at bs58 against wolf 0.2.21 / lupin 0.1.44 and 0.2.19 / 0.1.42 the same hour (release archives by digest, docs/audit/bs58-evidence/probes-control.txt and probes-subject.txt): identical on both pairs, word for word, same span. (owner: wolf-book#45 (the std root; successor of the closed #39) + wolf-book#58 (the unspellable `take`))
samples: PENDING ch07/ex7-5 [fail(E1003)] — blocker: borrow-escape checking reaches no static verdict. Re-measured at bs53 against wolf 0.2.17 / lupin 0.1.40, and identically against 0.2.16 / 0.1.38: wolf answers `cannot compile this yet — borrow expressions` at `resolve` (exit 4; `channel` resolves now, so the old second clause is gone), and lupin runs the program to exit 0 with no static rung. Re-measured at bs54 against wolf 0.2.18 / lupin 0.1.41: unchanged on both (`borrow expressions` @365..367, lupin exit 0). Re-measured at bs55 against wolf 0.2.19 / lupin 0.1.42: unchanged on both, same span. Re-measured at bs58 against wolf 0.2.21 / lupin 0.1.44 and 0.2.19 / 0.1.42 the same hour (release archives by digest, docs/audit/bs58-evidence/probes-control.txt and probes-subject.txt): identical on both pairs, word for word, same span. (owner: s33-channels-select, then s18-tier0-exclusivity)
samples: PENDING ch08/ex8-7 [run(exit=0, stdout="c a")] — blocker: TWO blockers, bisected at bs51 against wolf 0.2.16 / lupin 0.1.38 with two minimal programs rather than inferred from the exercise, and EACH MACHINE NOW SERVES THE HALF THE OTHER REFUSES. (1) The place write this row has always named — `pool[h].next = k` — LANDED ON THE COMPILER (s173: the pool is the base and the handle the index) and is still the interpreter's wall, in new words: lupin answers `unsupported: handle is not a `Map` key — a key is `str`, `int`, `char` or `bool` [type.map.key]` and exits 4, where wolf 0.2.16 runs the same program to exit 0. (2) A blocker that is NEW and is the COMPILER's: the LRU walk's `while cur != tail` compares two handles, and wolf answers `cannot compile this yet — `==` on a container, tuple or handle (no `Eq` for these this edition)` and exits 4, where lupin runs it. A conservatism line, not a rejection. bs51 predicted this row would flip on s173 and was wrong: s173 moved the half the row named and a second wall was behind it. Re-measured at bs53 (0.2.17 / 0.1.40) and at bs54 (0.2.18 / 0.1.41): both halves hold in the same words, the compiler's at the same span (@1926..1929); 0.2.18's pool-handle revival (eg01b) is about moves, not `Eq`. Re-measured at bs55 (0.2.19 / 0.1.42, and 0.2.18 / 0.1.41 the same hour): both halves identical, same span; 0.2.19's element claims (EG2) and header reads touch neither `Eq` nor map keys. Re-measured at bs58 against wolf 0.2.21 / lupin 0.1.44 and 0.2.19 / 0.1.42 the same hour (release archives by digest, docs/audit/bs58-evidence/probes-control.txt and probes-subject.txt): identical on both pairs, word for word, same span. (owner: wolf-book#60 (both halves, with the measurement))
